          dealing: "Deal 5 cards to each player. turn the next card (Dealer's last card) FACE-UP. This is the FLIP CARD.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Win the 'Game' pot by having the lowest points or going out, and win the 'Flip/Flop' pots by holding low cards.",
          gameplay: "1. Players reveal cards to claim Flip/Flop pots immediately.\n2. Standard Draw/Discard Rummy play ensues.\n3. Melds: Sets (3+ of a kind) or Runs (3+ sequential in suit).\n4. Dropping: At the start of your turn, you can place your cards face-up to 'Drop' (Knock). If you have the lowest point total, you win the Game Pot. If someone has lower/equal, you lose double ('Caught').",
          keyRules: [
            'No Jokers.',
            'Aces are always low (1).',
            "Pay to Play: You can't win a pot you didn't contribute to.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Check for 49/50 immediately. A starting hand of five face cards/10s is rare but instantly ends the game.',
          intermediate: "The Drop Threshold: Since face cards are 10, hand totals are high. If you have under 15 points early in the game, it is usually safe to 'Drop' and take the pot.",
          advanced: "Defensive Tunk: If you see a player has won the Flip and Flop stakes, they are 'freerolling' the Game pot. Play aggressively to Tunk out or Drop early to prevent them from sweeping the table and taking all three pots.",
          tips: [
            "Always keep a 'reserve' stake. Losing a 'Caught' drop costs double.",
            "Don't hold onto high cards hoping for a run. In Game, Flip, Flop, points are liabilities.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
